.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt MESH-NEIGHBOR-COUNT.PY 8
.Os MANET
.Sh NAME
.Nm mesh-neighbor-count.py
.Nd count distinct directly connected BATMAN neighbor nodes
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -batctl Ar path
.Op Fl -registry Ar path
.Op Fl h | Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
queries BATMAN neighbors on
.Li bat0
and prints an integer count of distinct peer nodes.
Run with permission to query BATMAN, normally as root.
Radio addresses are merged using the mesh registry so a peer connected
over several radios is counted once.
This counts direct neighbors, not all nodes reachable through the mesh.
.Pp
Zero or one neighbor address can be counted without the registry.
When several addresses are visible but their node identities are missing
or ambiguous, no integer is printed.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -batctl Ar path
BATMAN control executable; default
.Pa /usr/sbin/batctl .
.It Fl -registry Ar path
Registry to read; default
.Pa /var/run/mesh_node_registry .
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print help and exit.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/run/mesh_node_registry
Primary node MAC addresses and per-interface address lists.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
An exact count was printed, including zero.
.It 1
The BATMAN neighbor query failed or returned invalid data.
.It 2
Invalid arguments.
.It 3
Neighbors are present but their node identities cannot yet be resolved.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo mesh-neighbor-count.py
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mac-to-ip.sh 8
